# Symlinks to the prototype's / frontend's installs — recreate with the ln -sfn in README.md
node_modules

# Playwright run output. Regenerate by re-running the capture; nothing cites it.
test-results*/
report/
playwright-report/
.playwright-cli/

# Pixels stay out; provenance stays in.
#
# The old reason here was "16MB, and no finding cites one". That stopped being
# true the moment the report started rendering pictures under the findings. The
# real reason is that pixels regenerate from a pinned commit in about fifteen
# seconds on the frontend side and about three minutes on the prototype side,
# and that a fresh clone can be told exactly which files are missing and which
# command makes them, because the manifest that lists them IS committed.
#
# What is tracked: every manifest.json (sha256, dimensions, device scale factor,
# the commit the application was at) and every page model. Those are the record
# of what a ruling was made against, and they survive a fresh clone.
capture/screens/
*/capture/screens/
evidence/*/page/
evidence/*/crop/
evidence/*/html/
evidence/*/trace/
# The prototype harness writes its models and raw HTML beside the pixels when
# it is pointed at an evidence directory. Those are already tracked once, under
# harness/capture/, and one copy of a thing is the number to have.
evidence/*/model/
evidence/*/screens/
!evidence/*/manifest.json
